age>277</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15254285</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000544-Bockenstedt1"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bockenstedt</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>D-dimer in venous thromboembolism.</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>349</volume><fpage>1203</fpage><lpage>1204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14507947</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000544-Reyzer1"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reyzer</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsieh</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Korfmacher</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Caprioli</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Direct analysis of drug candidates in tissue by matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry.</article-title><source>J Mass Spectrom</source><volume>38</volume><fpage>1081</fpage><lpage>1092</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14595858</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000544-Wells3"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bormanis</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Guy</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Value of assessment of pretest probability of deep-vein thrombosis in clinical management.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>350</volume><fpage>1795</fpage><lpage>1798</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9428249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000544-Perrier1"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perrier</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Desmarais</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Miron</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>de Moerloose</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lepage</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Non-invasive diagnosis of venous thromboembolism in outpatients.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>353</volume><fpage>190</fpage><lpage>195</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9923874</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000544-Goldhaber3"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldhaber</surname><given-names>SZ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Pulmonary embolism.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>363</volume><fpage>1295</fpage><lpage>1305</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15094276</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="display-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig id="pone-0000544-g001" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000544.g001</object-id><label>Figure 1</label><caption><title>Computational pipeline used for analysis of direct MS data.</title><p>Successive computational steps were performed using a pipeline to normalize, average and transform mass spectral data, perform ANN analysis and establish performance metrics.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000544.g001"/></fig><fig id="pone-0000544-g002" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000544.g002</object-id><label>Figure 2</label><caption><title>Direct MS of serum.</title><p>Average spectra for patients with VTE (a) and without VTE (b) show differences in overall protein expression, with the internal spike protein denoted by an asterisk. The 500 signals selected by the ANOVA analysis are denoted by red circles, representing locations on the mass spectrum with differential protein expression between the two groups of patients (c).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000544.g002"/></fig><fig id="pone-0000544-g003" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000544.g003</object-id><label>Figure 3</label><caption><title>ROC characteristics for the direct MS method in the independent test set compared to standard D-dimer tests.</title><p>The optimized model shows comparable ROC curves in test set 1 (TST1) and test set 2 (TST2). D-Dimer by ELISA and immunoturbimetric assay results are plotted for all 76 patients in the cohort for comparison.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000544.g003"/></fig><fig id="pone-0000544-g004" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000544.g004</object-id><label>Figure 4</label><caption><title>Gel electrophoresis of serum from patients with and without VTE.</title><p>1-DGE of whole serum and depleted, conditioned serum was run on 4 VTE and 4 NonVTE patients (a). 2-DGE was performed on serum from patients with VTE and without VTE, with arrows pointing to a series of haptoglobin proteins with differential expression between VTE and NonVTE patients, displayed in two representative gels (b).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000544.g004"/></fig><table-wrap id="pone-0000544-t001" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000544.t001</object-id><label>Table 1</label><caption><title>Baseline characteristics of the patient cohort<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt101">&#x0002a;</xref>.</title></caption><graphic id="pone-0000544-t001-1" xlink:href="pone.0000544.t001"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" alternate-form-of="pone-0000544-t001-1"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/>